# Pins upgrade blocklist: one <key> per line to HOLD a toolchain or docker image pin of
# .ci/config/pins.json at its current value instead of tracking upstream.
#
# The key is the pin id after its colon (toolchain:npm -> npm, image:renet-ubuntu ->
# renet-ubuntu). Every toolchain and docker leaf names this file as its first `holds` file,
# and check:ci-pin-freshness refuses a line whose key no such leaf answers to.
#
# Write lines with `npm run pins -- hold <id> --reason "<why>" --expires YYYY-MM-DD`, never by
# hand. A newer major whose first release is past the grace in .ci/config/pin-major-grace.json
# turns check:ci-pin-freshness red unless the pin is bumped or held here WITH an expiry: an
# undated hold does not excuse an aged major.
#
# Do NOT hold a release that is merely too fresh: the release-age window in
# .ci/config/release-age.json defers it, and the deferral clears itself.
#
# Each entry needs a substantive BLOCKER reason, the same as every other suppression list here.
# Format, as `pins hold` writes it:
#
#   <key>  # BLOCKER: <why the pin is held back and when to revisit> (expires YYYY-MM-DD)
#
# Empty by default: nothing is held.

npm  # BLOCKER: npm 12 has not been evaluated against this repo's lockfile pass, overrides handling and ignore-scripts hardening; held so the operator schedules the major move rather than an unattended overnight session (expires 2026-11-14)

ci-node  # BLOCKER: the node images track the active LTS line 24; node 26 becomes LTS in late October 2026, and the move needs the CLI SEA build and the workers validated on 26, which the operator schedules (expires 2026-11-14)

node-alpine  # BLOCKER: the node images track the active LTS line 24; node 26 becomes LTS in late October 2026, and the move needs the CLI SEA build and the workers validated on 26, which the operator schedules (expires 2026-11-14)

renet-ubuntu  # BLOCKER: renet's runtime base tracks Ubuntu LTS 24.04; a 26.x base needs a renet rebuild and the KVM e2e distro matrix before it moves, which the operator schedules (expires 2026-11-14)

cuda  # BLOCKER: BLOCKER: the narration image runs VoxCPM2 and Qwen3-ASR on a WSL GPU host, and a CUDA 13.4 runtime base needs a GPU build plus narration smoke run that no unattended session can do; the 13.0.1 base stays until the operator schedules it (expires 2026-11-14)
